<!--
    AArch64 system-register names and Apple's proprietary instructions
    (SLEIGH spec fix, no option).

    Issue: the AARCH64 spec named 304 system registers; every other MRS/MSR,
    including Apple's implementation-defined ones (HID0_EL1, SPRR_CONFIG_EL1,
    GXF_STATUS_EL1, ...), lifted to UnkSytemRegRead(3,0,0xf,0,0). Apple's
    instructions in the 0x0020xxxx space did not decode at all: WKDMC was a
    `NotYetImplemented` placeholder and GENTER a bad-instruction halt, so an
    iOS kernelcache function stopped at its first GENTER.

    Stage / sub-stage: P1 decode-table. `AARCH64_sysregs.sinc` /
    `AARCH64_sysregs_cop.sinc` add 1,612 registers (LLVM's architectural
    table and the Asahi m1n1 Apple table); `AARCH64_apple.sinc` decodes
    MUL53LO/HI, WKDMC/D, GENTER, GEXIT and SDSB as opaque pcodeops.

      mrs  x0, s3_0_c15_c0_0      ; HID0_EL1 (Apple)
      mrs  x1, s3_0_c0_c6_2       ; ID_AA64ISAR2_EL1 (architectural)
      add  x0, x0, x1
      msr  s3_6_c15_c1_0, x0      ; SPRR_CONFIG_EL1 (Apple)
      wkdmc x0, x1
      genter #0
      ret
-->
